Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:28:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] marianos-azure-headless 1.10.0rc6 (tests only): the
 Coupons row is read only when its list loaded, and its verdict holds through
 the run (OR-04)

Seven of twelve runs before 1.10.0rc6 recorded the Coupons page (CSV row 0) as read with 0 coupons when the
page had been rendered before its list loaded. These tests use the two real Coupons pages stored on
2026-11-16 (loaded with 24 cards; the site's loading indicator, no count, no card) and derived pages for what
no stored page shows (a loaded empty list; a count without cards; a product page still loading). They state:
three readings of the list (loaded with cards, loaded empty, not loaded); a page not loaded asked again
within its bounds; the answers and the verdict kept across a restart; an unread Coupons route keeps a run of
the whole list from complete (G3, the dataset label, the coverage file); a product page still loading proves
no coupon absent. Expected to fail on 1.10.0rc5 (12 tests); the control passes on both.
---
